From 8987a8db790fbd9d0f2557a875225779c677c129 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: adbtrr_work8_fin_tc <adbtrr_work8_fin_tc@local>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 06:14:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] os/kernel/group: Add ASSERT hitting test case for
 group_foreachchild

group_foreachchild() dereferences the "group" argument right after
DEBUGASSERT(group), so a NULL group is a caller contract violation.

Add a negative test case which calls group_foreachchild() with a NULL
task group from kernel context so that the assertion in
os/kernel/group/group_foreachchild.c is executed.

 - os/drivers/os_api_test/kernel/test_assert_group.c : kernel side
   helper reached through the TESTIOC_ASSERT_GROUP ioctl.
 - apps/examples/testcase/le_tc/kernel/tc_assert_group.c : user side
   test case. The ioctl is not expected to return, so a return from it
   is reported as a test case failure.

The test case is controlled by CONFIG_TC_KERNEL_ASSERT_GROUP which
defaults to n and depends on CONFIG_DEBUG, because DEBUGASSERT() is
compiled out when CONFIG_DEBUG is disabled. It crashes the board by
design and must be enabled alone.
